WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.133 --> 00:00:02.100
-Now,
welcome back to the show.

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:05.033
I'm so happy that you're here.

00:00:05.033 --> 00:00:09.434
I want to just kind of recap
what a year it's been for you.

00:00:09.434 --> 00:00:11.801
-Yeah.
-Because we're friends

00:00:11.801 --> 00:00:14.901
and we text each other
every now and then.

00:00:14.901 --> 00:00:17.467
-Yeah. No, we do text.
-We do.

00:00:17.467 --> 00:00:20.167
-It took me a long time
to get that phone number.

00:00:20.167 --> 00:00:22.200
-I know.
-I had to battle it out.

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:24.200
-Did you really?
-And now my daughter is here,

00:00:24.200 --> 00:00:26.968
kicked me out
of my dressing room.

00:00:26.968 --> 00:00:29.501
-Your beautiful little daughter?
-Yeah. She goes --

00:00:29.501 --> 00:00:30.801
I was, like,
standing in there, and she goes,

00:00:30.801 --> 00:00:32.734
"Do you mind shutting
that door?" and made me go.

00:00:32.734 --> 00:00:33.868
[ Laughter ]
-[ Indistinct ]

00:00:33.868 --> 00:00:35.767
-Yeah, but isn't that fun,
though?

00:00:35.767 --> 00:00:41.100
When you first came on,
you were just booking clubs

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:42.267
and hoping that
you'd book clubs.

00:00:42.267 --> 00:00:43.567
-Oh, yeah.
-You sent me a text.

00:00:43.567 --> 00:00:44.834
I go,
"Where are you playing tonight?

00:00:44.834 --> 00:00:46.767
Like, what are you doing?"
You go, "No big deal.

00:00:46.767 --> 00:00:50.834
I'm just doing the
Bridgestone Arena in Nashville."

00:00:50.834 --> 00:00:55.267
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:55.267 --> 00:01:00.267
-You broke the attendance record
with almost 20,000 people.

00:01:00.267 --> 00:01:02.501
This is where they play hockey.
This is where they do --

00:01:02.501 --> 00:01:03.834
-Yeah, yeah.
-Nate.

00:01:03.834 --> 00:01:05.234
-It was -- It's crazy, dude.

00:01:05.234 --> 00:01:07.033
-And your special's
the biggest show

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:09.100
in the history
of Amazon Prime,

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:10.534
which is --
It's all happening.

00:01:10.534 --> 00:01:12.868
It's all so -- Yesterday,
in the last two days,

00:01:12.868 --> 00:01:15.634
three sold-out shows
at Radio City Music Hall.

00:01:15.634 --> 00:01:17.934
I mean, congrats, buddy.
I can't --

00:01:17.934 --> 00:01:19.767
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you. Thank you.

00:01:19.767 --> 00:01:21.033
By the way,
that Bridgestone,

00:01:21.033 --> 00:01:23.434
I stole one of the chairs
from Bridgestone.

00:01:23.434 --> 00:01:26.100
-What do you mean you stole one?
-Because I have the record.

00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:28.567
So if I take one
of the chairs home,

00:01:28.567 --> 00:01:30.734
no one can break that record.
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:30.734 --> 00:01:33.634
-That is brilliant.
-Yeah.

00:01:33.634 --> 00:01:35.067
-That is absolutely...

00:01:35.067 --> 00:01:36.667
-You just cut right to it.
-You cut -- Yeah.

00:01:36.667 --> 00:01:38.367
-Yeah. Yeah.
-It's unbeatable.

00:01:38.367 --> 00:01:40.300
The special is --
I think my favorite joke

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:41.801
is the house joke.

00:01:41.801 --> 00:01:45.000
You have -- You're living
in the house backwards.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:46.133
-Yeah, yeah.
-But it's such a great --

00:01:46.133 --> 00:01:47.701
I said the punchline.
It doesn't matter.

00:01:47.701 --> 00:01:49.300
Watch it. It's worth it.

00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:52.634
But also the fact that it blows
people's mind that you're clean,

00:01:52.634 --> 00:01:54.200
by the way.
-Yeah.

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:56.634
-I watched it with my --
I watched it by myself.

00:01:56.634 --> 00:01:58.434
I think I texted you.
I said, "Here's my notes.

00:01:58.434 --> 00:01:59.467
I love this.
This is my favorite thing."

00:01:59.467 --> 00:02:01.033
And then I watched it
with my dad

00:02:01.033 --> 00:02:03.133
because it's something
I can watch with my dad.

00:02:03.133 --> 00:02:05.868
So he was crying laughing.
It's so great.

00:02:05.868 --> 00:02:07.434
You can watch it
with everybody.

00:02:07.434 --> 00:02:09.701
We were laughing so hard.
You said because your dad,

00:02:09.701 --> 00:02:12.033
I think, found a screen door
on the side of the road.

00:02:12.033 --> 00:02:13.601
-Yeah.
-And then saw it.

00:02:13.601 --> 00:02:15.133
-Put it in -- Yeah.
Put it in our house

00:02:15.133 --> 00:02:17.334
and he put it on the wrong way

00:02:17.334 --> 00:02:19.767
because the handle was on --
the handle is on this side

00:02:19.767 --> 00:02:21.434
and the screen door
is on this side.

00:02:21.434 --> 00:02:24.033
So if you came in our house
you had to go like --

00:02:24.033 --> 00:02:25.701
you had to do that.
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:25.701 --> 00:02:26.801
-And it was my mom.

00:02:26.801 --> 00:02:28.567
My mom just wanted
a screen door

00:02:28.567 --> 00:02:30.567
because she wanted it
to be normal.

00:02:30.567 --> 00:02:32.901
She was like, "A normal family
in a home..."

00:02:32.901 --> 00:02:34.801
This was the first home
they bought,

00:02:34.801 --> 00:02:37.767
and it was in Old Hickory
and it was a two-bedroom home.

00:02:37.767 --> 00:02:39.434
tiny, and she's like,
"A screen door,

00:02:39.434 --> 00:02:42.234
we'd be a normal family
for two seconds.

00:02:42.234 --> 00:02:43.868
Just give us a screen door."

00:02:43.868 --> 00:02:45.100
And then my dad gets it

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:47.601
and it's just the most
not normal screen door.

00:02:47.601 --> 00:02:49.634
-[ Laughs ] She still didn't get
what she wanted.

00:02:49.634 --> 00:02:51.067
-Still did not get what she --
I don't know.

00:02:51.067 --> 00:02:52.467
She still
doesn't have a screen door.

00:02:52.467 --> 00:02:53.801
-But how is your dad doing?

00:02:53.801 --> 00:02:55.868
I know he's been opening up
for some of your shows.

00:02:55.868 --> 00:02:58.334
-He was just here. He does --
I mean, he's been great.

00:02:58.334 --> 00:03:00.267
You know, it's every
little boy's dream,

00:03:00.267 --> 00:03:02.234
travel with your dad when you're
44 years old.

00:03:02.234 --> 00:03:04.467
[ Laughter ]

00:03:04.467 --> 00:03:06.467
It's...
-That's it. Wow.

00:03:06.467 --> 00:03:08.567
It really is a dream, yeah.
-I got a tour bus with

00:03:08.567 --> 00:03:11.567
a CPAP machine hooked up, so...
[ Laughter ]

00:03:11.567 --> 00:03:13.601
...it's pretty good times.

00:03:13.601 --> 00:03:17.167
We're out there mixing it up.
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:17.167 --> 00:03:18.868
You said that he's like
a prankster, right?

00:03:18.868 --> 00:03:19.767
Your dad?
-Oh, yeah.

00:03:19.767 --> 00:03:21.734
He did one to my brother.

00:03:21.734 --> 00:03:23.267
His own son.

00:03:23.267 --> 00:03:27.767
And Derek was getting all
his doors painted in his house,

00:03:27.767 --> 00:03:29.133
so he took all the door
knobs off

00:03:29.133 --> 00:03:31.801
and laid them in the living
room floor on a sheet.

00:03:31.801 --> 00:03:33.767
And my dad went
and bought one extra doorknob

00:03:33.767 --> 00:03:37.834
and put it in there.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.834 --> 00:03:39.734
Yeah.
-Just to slowly drive him crazy.

00:03:39.734 --> 00:03:42.801
Your brother's like, "Wait."
-Well, he came back and like,

00:03:42.801 --> 00:03:45.167
I mean, if you want to drive
someone crazy, do that.

00:03:45.167 --> 00:03:47.167
Like, it's like,
"Where's the other door?"

00:03:47.167 --> 00:03:49.100
Like, we're missing...

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:50.734
They're missing
a whole other door.

00:03:50.734 --> 00:03:51.934
-It's a really funny prank.

00:03:51.934 --> 00:03:53.133
-They almost got divorced
over it.

00:03:53.133 --> 00:03:55.634
It's like, "What,
are you hiding doors from me?

00:03:55.634 --> 00:03:56.868
What else
are you hiding from me?"

00:03:56.868 --> 00:04:00.267
You know? Yeah.
-Things are going super well.

00:04:00.267 --> 00:04:03.267
You started this new company
called The Nateland.

00:04:03.267 --> 00:04:05.133
-The Nateland Company.
-Nateland.

00:04:05.133 --> 00:04:07.501
-Nateland. And it's
a production company.

00:04:07.501 --> 00:04:10.701
You're making family-friendly
comedy specials

00:04:10.701 --> 00:04:13.000
on YouTube right now.
-Yeah, right now the showcase is

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:14.734
on Nateland Entertainment,
YouTube.

00:04:14.734 --> 00:04:17.868
The showcase is out.
-Nateland?

00:04:17.868 --> 00:04:19.400
-It sounds as if
you said Nate-lind.

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:21.667
-Nateland. I say Nateland.

00:04:21.667 --> 00:04:24.567
-No, you didn't.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:24.567 --> 00:04:26.300
-When?
-I think he said Nate-lind.

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:27.868
I said Nateland,
and you go "Nate-lind."

00:04:27.868 --> 00:04:29.267
And I go,
"Oh, was I saying it wrong?"

00:04:29.267 --> 00:04:31.801
-Well, that might be my accent.

00:04:31.801 --> 00:04:33.801
That shouldn't count
as me mispronouncing it.

00:04:33.801 --> 00:04:35.267
You should be able to
read through and go,

00:04:35.267 --> 00:04:37.000
"He doesn't even know
what he's talking about."

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:38.567
Like, that's --
-No, I just didn't know if

00:04:38.567 --> 00:04:39.734
I was saying it wrong.

00:04:39.734 --> 00:04:40.901
I wanted to make sure
I'm saying it correctly.

00:04:40.901 --> 00:04:42.868
-I think anything I say
you could be like,

00:04:42.868 --> 00:04:44.167
"You probably said it right."

00:04:44.167 --> 00:04:46.434
I told you I think you say our
last name correct

00:04:46.434 --> 00:04:47.901
with "Bar-got-see"

00:04:47.901 --> 00:04:49.834
and I think we say
it wrong as a family.

00:04:49.834 --> 00:04:52.767
[ Laughter ]
"Bar-get-see."

00:04:52.767 --> 00:04:55.300
-For years I've been
calling you Nate "Bar-got-see."

00:04:55.300 --> 00:04:58.334
-Yeah, and I just went with that
'cause you were so big

00:04:58.334 --> 00:05:00.801
it was easier just to --
[ Laughter ]

00:05:00.801 --> 00:05:04.267
It's just easier to do
whatever you choose. You go...

00:05:04.267 --> 00:05:05.701
-I don't want
to name you, though,

00:05:05.701 --> 00:05:07.534
but your name is Nate Bargatze.

00:05:07.534 --> 00:05:09.634
-Marc Maron once called me Nick,

00:05:09.634 --> 00:05:11.100
and I was like,
"I'll just be Nick."

00:05:11.100 --> 00:05:13.868
Like, it's already -- It was
enough people that was Nick,

00:05:13.868 --> 00:05:17.467
I was like, "I'll just go
with whatever's out there."

00:05:17.467 --> 00:05:20.133
-The tour, the special,
the new company --

00:05:20.133 --> 00:05:22.234
you got a lot going on.

00:05:22.234 --> 00:05:23.801
Is it hard to keep
track of everything?

00:05:23.801 --> 00:05:25.534
-Yeah. Yeah. I mean,
it's all getting crazy now.

00:05:25.534 --> 00:05:28.000
And we live, you know --
it's like as I get older,

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:29.033
it's like, I don't know.

00:05:29.033 --> 00:05:30.367
Like, we live
in a neighborhood.

00:05:30.367 --> 00:05:32.801
We live in a cul de sac,
and we're the house at the top,

00:05:32.801 --> 00:05:35.901
so we are the leaders
of the cul de sac.

00:05:35.901 --> 00:05:37.801
But, like, all my neighbors
are all like,

00:05:37.801 --> 00:05:39.300
they all have real jobs.

00:05:39.300 --> 00:05:40.501
You know, when you're, like,
around people with real jobs?

00:05:40.501 --> 00:05:42.567
Like, I don't know
anything about taxes.

00:05:42.567 --> 00:05:45.501
I get asked about
my property taxes every day.

00:05:45.501 --> 00:05:47.701
Just some guy, you know,
and I'll just say --

00:05:47.701 --> 00:05:48.968
I just say,
"They are what they are."

00:05:48.968 --> 00:05:51.000
You know, you just...
-That's a good answer.

00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:52.801
-I told --
One guy wouldn't let up

00:05:52.801 --> 00:05:54.067
because he was moving
to Nashville,

00:05:54.067 --> 00:05:54.901
and I was like, "100 --"

00:05:54.901 --> 00:05:56.334
I just told him $100,000,

00:05:56.334 --> 00:05:58.968
and he was so mad.

00:05:58.968 --> 00:06:02.567
So I thought,
"Alright, too high."

00:06:02.567 --> 00:06:06.167
And I said, "$85 a month."

00:06:06.167 --> 00:06:08.834
And he was like, "What?"
And I go, "What?

00:06:08.834 --> 00:06:11.701
What do you want them to be?"
[ Laughter ]

00:06:11.701 --> 00:06:13.000
Do you see my wife here?

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:14.400
I don't know if we own
or rent our home.

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:15.868
I've never asked
any of these questions."

00:06:15.868 --> 00:06:17.167
Like, yeah.

00:06:17.167 --> 00:06:18.067
-You're not supposed to know
those things.

00:06:18.067 --> 00:06:19.534
-I don't know this stuff.
-No.

00:06:19.534 --> 00:06:21.467
Do you have, like, a --
Do you have a lawyer?

00:06:21.467 --> 00:06:23.701
-No. I always think
you should want a lawyer.

00:06:23.701 --> 00:06:26.601
Don't you see on TV?
Did you see that growing up?

00:06:26.601 --> 00:06:28.400
Everybody'd be like,
"Call my lawyer."

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:29.667
-Yeah.
-And then they --

00:06:29.667 --> 00:06:32.000
And you're like, "Are we
supposed to have a lawyer?"

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:34.534
Like, I don't like...
I just call him,

00:06:34.534 --> 00:06:36.467
I get my lawyer on the phone.
They have one.

00:06:36.467 --> 00:06:39.834
I've never had one.

00:06:39.834 --> 00:06:41.601
I don't know
any court stuff either.

00:06:41.601 --> 00:06:44.534
Like, I think I got --
I got to miss out

00:06:44.534 --> 00:06:46.467
on jury duty because of COVID.

00:06:46.467 --> 00:06:48.567
But I was very scared
about going

00:06:48.567 --> 00:06:51.000
because I'd never understand
that the jury is there,

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:52.367
and the judge tells the jury,

00:06:52.367 --> 00:06:55.100
"Alright, well,
don't remember that part."

00:06:55.100 --> 00:06:56.667
And you're like,
"That's the only part

00:06:56.667 --> 00:06:58.067
I'm going to remember now."
[ Laughter ]

00:06:58.067 --> 00:07:01.434
Like, it's like the main...
-You can't tell me to not --

00:07:01.434 --> 00:07:03.667
-"Remember when he said
he did it for sure?

00:07:03.667 --> 00:07:05.567
Don't remember that part."
You're like, "Alright."

00:07:05.567 --> 00:07:08.367
-If you want a jury,
don't never have Nate Bargatze

00:07:08.367 --> 00:07:11.367
or "Bar-got-see" on your jury.

00:07:11.367 --> 00:07:14.100
Nate Bargatze, his special,
"Nate Bargatze:

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:16.734
Hello World" is streaming
now on Prime Video.

00:07:16.734 --> 00:07:19.000
You won't be --
It's unbelievable.

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:20.601
It really is an all-timer.

00:07:20.601 --> 00:07:22.701
I'm so happy for you, buddy.
Thanks so much for coming back.

00:07:22.701 --> 00:07:23.968
-You're a big part of it.
-I love you, buddy.

00:07:23.968 --> 00:07:26.400
-Thank you. Love you, buddy.
-Stick around.

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:27.868
Be right back with more
"Tonight Show."

00:07:27.868 --> 00:07:29.467
Come on back, everybody!

